          "name": "Amazon WorkMail Test Availability Configuration",
          "request": {
            "name": "Amazon WorkMail Test Availability Configuration",
            "description": {
              "content": "<p>Performs a test on an availability provider to ensure that access is allowed. For EWS, it verifies the provided credentials can be used to successfully log in. For Lambda, it verifies that the Lambda function can be invoked and that the resource access policy was configured to deny anonymous access. An anonymous invocation is one done without providing either a <code>SourceArn</code> or <code>SourceAccount</code> header.</p> <note> <p>The request must contain either one provider definition (<code>EwsProvider</code> or <code>LambdaProvider</code>) or the <code>DomainName</code> parameter. If the <code>DomainName</code> parameter is provided, the configuration stored under the <code>DomainName</code> will be tested.</p> </note>",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
